1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,524
Somewhere in the North Sea,

2
00:00:02,524 --> 00:00:05,000
a platform pumps oil from beneath the

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,110
seabed.

4
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,010
The money it earns ends up in

5
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:10,386
one of the largest investment funds on

6
00:00:10,386 --> 00:00:11,223
Earth.

7
00:00:11,483 --> 00:00:13,959
Norway's oil fund was worth 22 trillion

8
00:00:13,959 --> 00:00:17,963
kroner at the end of September 2026.

9
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:20,310
Divide that by every person in the

10
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:20,881
country,

11
00:00:20,881 --> 00:00:23,580
and it comes to about 3.9 million

12
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:24,771
kroner each.

13
00:00:25,017 --> 00:00:25,946
Through that fund,

14
00:00:25,946 --> 00:00:29,447
Norway owns on average 1.5 percent of

15
00:00:29,447 --> 00:00:32,667
every listed company in the world.

16
00:00:32,827 --> 00:00:35,784
7,201 companies,

17
00:00:35,784 --> 00:00:38,164
in 68 countries.

18
00:00:38,417 --> 00:00:41,047
Plenty of countries have found oil.

19
00:00:41,297 --> 00:00:43,667
Few have ended up like this.

20
00:00:43,837 --> 00:00:46,927
So what did Norway do differently?

21
00:00:47,247 --> 00:00:50,183
This is The Hidden Economics.

22
00:00:53,617 --> 00:00:55,105
Before the oil,

23
00:00:55,105 --> 00:00:57,839
Norway lived from the sea and the

24
00:00:57,839 --> 00:00:58,977
mountains.

25
00:00:58,977 --> 00:01:01,407
Fishing boats worked the coast.

26
00:01:01,617 --> 00:01:04,238
By the nineteen-fifties its merchant fleet

27
00:01:04,238 --> 00:01:06,620
was described as the third largest in

28
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:07,697
the world.

29
00:01:08,067 --> 00:01:10,465
And In 1905,

30
00:01:10,465 --> 00:01:13,559
Norsk Hydro began turning waterfalls into

31
00:01:13,559 --> 00:01:15,191
fertiliser.

32
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,695
It was a modest,

33
00:01:16,695 --> 00:01:18,361
hard-working economy,

34
00:01:18,361 --> 00:01:20,860
but not an especially rich one.

35
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:23,013
In 1970,

36
00:01:23,013 --> 00:01:25,895
Norway's income per person was only about

37
00:01:25,895 --> 00:01:27,312
four-fifths of Sweden's,

38
00:01:27,312 --> 00:01:29,353
and behind Denmark's too.

39
00:01:32,817 --> 00:01:35,985
Few believed there was oil under Norway's

40
00:01:35,985 --> 00:01:37,737
seabed at all.

41
00:01:37,757 --> 00:01:39,502
In 1958,

42
00:01:39,502 --> 00:01:42,026
the national geological survey told the

43
00:01:42,026 --> 00:01:43,708
government the chances could be

44
00:01:43,708 --> 00:01:44,939
discounted.

45
00:01:45,183 --> 00:01:45,795
Still,

46
00:01:45,795 --> 00:01:49,613
Norway claimed its continental shelf.

47
00:01:49,743 --> 00:01:51,731
In 1965,

48
00:01:51,731 --> 00:01:53,888
it agreed a median line through the

49
00:01:53,888 --> 00:01:56,020
North Sea with Britain and Denmark,

50
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,942
and handed out its first 22 production

51
00:01:58,942 --> 00:02:00,261
licences.

52
00:02:00,517 --> 00:02:03,377
The first wells came up dry.

53
00:02:03,637 --> 00:02:04,129
Then,

54
00:02:04,129 --> 00:02:07,317
just before Christmas 1969,

55
00:02:07,317 --> 00:02:10,686
the American company Phillips Petroleum

56
00:02:10,686 --> 00:02:13,877
reported a find called Ekofisk.

57
00:02:14,207 --> 00:02:15,248
At the time,

58
00:02:15,248 --> 00:02:17,650
it was the largest offshore oil field

59
00:02:17,650 --> 00:02:19,852
ever discovered.

60
00:02:20,117 --> 00:02:23,878
Oil started flowing from Ekofisk in June

61
00:02:23,878 --> 00:02:26,667
1971.

62
00:02:26,917 --> 00:02:30,103
Norway had become an oil nation almost

63
00:02:30,103 --> 00:02:31,572
overnight.

64
00:02:35,017 --> 00:02:38,159
Norway's first big decision was about

65
00:02:38,159 --> 00:02:39,387
control.

66
00:02:39,667 --> 00:02:41,821
In 1971,

67
00:02:41,821 --> 00:02:44,649
parliament adopted ten principles,

68
00:02:44,649 --> 00:02:47,218
later called the oil commandments,

69
00:02:47,218 --> 00:02:49,813
to keep the resource under national

70
00:02:49,813 --> 00:02:52,407
control and the industry serving the

71
00:02:52,407 --> 00:02:53,526
country.

72
00:02:53,783 --> 00:02:55,674
In 1972,

73
00:02:55,674 --> 00:02:57,929
it created a state oil company,

74
00:02:57,929 --> 00:02:58,589
Statoil,

75
00:02:58,589 --> 00:03:00,161
and a regulator,

76
00:03:00,161 --> 00:03:02,583
the Petroleum Directorate.

77
00:03:03,123 --> 00:03:05,144
In 1985,

78
00:03:05,144 --> 00:03:08,066
the state also began holding direct stakes

79
00:03:08,066 --> 00:03:09,883
in oil fields itself.

80
00:03:10,413 --> 00:03:14,060
Today the government still owns 67 percent

81
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:15,966
of Statoil's successor,

82
00:03:15,966 --> 00:03:17,394
Equinor.

83
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:20,500
The second decision was tax.

84
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,687
Oil companies pay the normal 22 percent

85
00:03:23,687 --> 00:03:24,796
company tax,

86
00:03:24,796 --> 00:03:28,257
plus a special petroleum tax of 71.8

87
00:03:28,257 --> 00:03:29,310
percent.

88
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:30,312
Together,

89
00:03:30,312 --> 00:03:32,701
the state takes 78 percent of the

90
00:03:32,701 --> 00:03:34,581
profit at the margin.

91
00:03:34,817 --> 00:03:36,764
So the oil pays the state three

92
00:03:36,764 --> 00:03:37,376
ways:

93
00:03:37,376 --> 00:03:39,852
taxes on company profits,

94
00:03:39,852 --> 00:03:41,772
its own share of the fields,

95
00:03:41,772 --> 00:03:44,597
and dividends from Equinor.

96
00:03:48,050 --> 00:03:50,690
Those streams are enormous.

97
00:03:50,690 --> 00:03:52,405
In 2022,

98
00:03:52,405 --> 00:03:54,245
when energy prices spiked,

99
00:03:54,245 --> 00:03:56,312
the state's net cash flow from petroleum

100
00:03:56,312 --> 00:03:59,950
hit a record about 1.3 trillion kroner.

101
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:02,407
Even in a calmer year like last

102
00:04:02,407 --> 00:04:02,862
year,

103
00:04:02,862 --> 00:04:06,050
it was 664 billion kroner.

104
00:04:06,317 --> 00:04:08,834
Oil and gas made up 57 percent

105
00:04:08,834 --> 00:04:12,041
of the value of everything Norway exported

106
00:04:12,041 --> 00:04:14,467
in 2025.

107
00:04:14,777 --> 00:04:18,351
And through about 8,800 kilometres of

108
00:04:18,351 --> 00:04:19,488
pipelines,

109
00:04:19,488 --> 00:04:22,087
Norway's gas now covers more than 30

110
00:04:22,087 --> 00:04:24,175
percent of all the gas used in

111
00:04:24,175 --> 00:04:26,864
the European Union and Britain.

112
00:04:27,117 --> 00:04:30,586
That much money arriving that fast is

113
00:04:30,586 --> 00:04:32,227
dangerous.

114
00:04:32,457 --> 00:04:33,959
Spend it all at home,

115
00:04:33,959 --> 00:04:35,970
and wages and prices surge,

116
00:04:35,970 --> 00:04:37,473
the currency soars,

117
00:04:37,473 --> 00:04:40,528
and every other industry struggles to

118
00:04:40,528 --> 00:04:41,637
compete.

119
00:04:42,067 --> 00:04:45,436
Economists call it the resource curse.

120
00:04:48,883 --> 00:04:51,541
Norway's answer was to park the money

121
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:52,643
abroad.

122
00:04:52,643 --> 00:04:54,380
In 1990,

123
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:57,073
parliament created a petroleum fund.

124
00:04:57,173 --> 00:04:59,575
In May 1996,

125
00:04:59,575 --> 00:05:02,313
the first almost 2 billion kroner went

126
00:05:02,313 --> 00:05:03,171
in.

127
00:05:03,417 --> 00:05:05,727
Parliament sets the rules.

128
00:05:05,737 --> 00:05:07,857
The finance ministry owns the fund on

129
00:05:07,857 --> 00:05:09,457
the people's behalf.

130
00:05:09,457 --> 00:05:11,498
And the central bank's investment arm,

131
00:05:11,498 --> 00:05:13,622
created In 1998,

132
00:05:13,622 --> 00:05:15,047
manages it.

133
00:05:15,117 --> 00:05:16,830
One rule matters most:

134
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:19,209
the fund is not allowed to invest

135
00:05:19,209 --> 00:05:20,999
in Norway at all.

136
00:05:21,250 --> 00:05:23,750
Then the money compounded.

137
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,568
Here is the value of the fund

138
00:05:25,568 --> 00:05:27,035
at the end of each year,

139
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,910
in billions of kroner.

140
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:32,197
The line barely moves in the beginning,

141
00:05:32,197 --> 00:05:33,143
then it climbs,

142
00:05:33,143 --> 00:05:33,846
and climbs,

143
00:05:33,846 --> 00:05:36,143
past twenty thousand billion.

144
00:05:36,383 --> 00:05:38,753
Here is the surprising part.

145
00:05:38,753 --> 00:05:41,142
According to the fund's manager,

146
00:05:41,142 --> 00:05:43,313
the oil money paid in accounts for

147
00:05:43,313 --> 00:05:45,843
less than half of its value today.

148
00:05:46,213 --> 00:05:48,056
The rest has been earned by the

149
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:50,038
investments themselves.

150
00:05:53,483 --> 00:05:55,027
Most of the money,

151
00:05:55,027 --> 00:05:57,146
about 72 percent,

152
00:05:57,146 --> 00:05:58,793
is in shares.

153
00:05:58,873 --> 00:06:01,203
Around a quarter is in bonds.

154
00:06:01,263 --> 00:06:03,277
A small slice is in property and

155
00:06:03,277 --> 00:06:06,562
in renewable energy infrastructure.

156
00:06:06,817 --> 00:06:09,897
And it is spread across the planet.

157
00:06:10,017 --> 00:06:11,169
The biggest share,

158
00:06:11,169 --> 00:06:13,331
52.9 percent,

159
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:16,517
is invested in the United States.

160
00:06:16,737 --> 00:06:19,887
Its largest single holdings are Nvidia,

161
00:06:19,887 --> 00:06:22,222
Apple and Alphabet.

162
00:06:22,483 --> 00:06:24,314
Since it began buying shares,

163
00:06:24,314 --> 00:06:26,862
the fund has returned an average of

164
00:06:26,862 --> 00:06:29,087
6.6 percent a year,

165
00:06:29,087 --> 00:06:33,003
or 4.3 percent after inflation and costs.

166
00:06:33,003 --> 00:06:34,805
But it is not a smooth ride:

167
00:06:34,805 --> 00:06:37,267
it lost minus 23 percent in the

168
00:06:37,267 --> 00:06:38,564
financial crisis,

169
00:06:38,564 --> 00:06:42,592
and minus 14 percent in 2022.

170
00:06:46,050 --> 00:06:48,450
The real secret is a rule about

171
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:49,500
spending.

172
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,353
Since 2001,

173
00:06:51,353 --> 00:06:53,563
the government may only take out,

174
00:06:53,563 --> 00:06:54,434
over time,

175
00:06:54,434 --> 00:06:56,444
what the fund is expected to earn

176
00:06:56,444 --> 00:06:58,160
after inflation.

177
00:06:58,260 --> 00:07:00,087
That was set at 4 percent,

178
00:07:00,087 --> 00:07:03,696
and cut to 3 percent in 2017.

179
00:07:03,950 --> 00:07:05,777
In the budget for this year,

180
00:07:05,777 --> 00:07:09,199
the government planned to use 579 billion

181
00:07:09,199 --> 00:07:10,795
kroner of oil money,

182
00:07:10,795 --> 00:07:14,100
about 2.8 percent of the fund.

183
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:17,099
The IMF estimates that money from the

184
00:07:17,099 --> 00:07:19,241
fund now pays for about a quarter

185
00:07:19,241 --> 00:07:21,270
of all public spending.

186
00:07:21,517 --> 00:07:24,737
Spending only the return means the capital

187
00:07:24,737 --> 00:07:26,947
is never used up.

188
00:07:27,047 --> 00:07:29,733
The oil is converted into shares,

189
00:07:29,733 --> 00:07:31,926
bonds and buildings around the world,

190
00:07:31,926 --> 00:07:34,143
and Norwegians who are not yet born

191
00:07:34,143 --> 00:07:35,975
will share in it too.

192
00:07:36,217 --> 00:07:39,187
It also protects the economy at home.

193
00:07:39,247 --> 00:07:41,864
Because spending is tied to the fund,

194
00:07:41,864 --> 00:07:43,688
not to this year's oil price,

195
00:07:43,688 --> 00:07:46,332
the IMF concluded that the rule and

196
00:07:46,332 --> 00:07:49,240
the fund would largely insulate Norway

197
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:51,691
from a fall in oil revenue.

198
00:07:55,150 --> 00:07:56,380
Oil is still big,

199
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:59,240
but it is not the whole story.

200
00:07:59,490 --> 00:08:01,631
In 2025,

201
00:08:01,631 --> 00:08:04,211
about four-fifths of Norway's output came

202
00:08:04,211 --> 00:08:06,584
from the mainland economy:

203
00:08:06,584 --> 00:08:07,848
the industries,

204
00:08:07,848 --> 00:08:10,918
services and public sector outside oil,

205
00:08:10,918 --> 00:08:12,550
gas and shipping.

206
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:16,163
That economy runs on an unusual model.

207
00:08:16,313 --> 00:08:18,613
About half of workers belong to a

208
00:08:18,613 --> 00:08:19,673
union.

209
00:08:19,853 --> 00:08:20,852
In wage talks,

210
00:08:20,852 --> 00:08:22,644
the industries that compete

211
00:08:22,644 --> 00:08:25,435
internationally negotiate first,

212
00:08:25,435 --> 00:08:27,970
and everyone else follows their lead,

213
00:08:27,970 --> 00:08:29,762
so pay keeps in step with what

214
00:08:29,762 --> 00:08:31,899
exporters can afford.

215
00:08:32,150 --> 00:08:34,341
Income is spread evenly,

216
00:08:34,341 --> 00:08:36,050
and trust is high.

217
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,981
In the latest OECD survey,

218
00:08:37,981 --> 00:08:40,923
57 percent of Norwegians said they trusted

219
00:08:40,923 --> 00:08:42,684
their national government,

220
00:08:42,684 --> 00:08:45,780
against 40 percent across the OECD.

221
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:48,161
Trust makes long-term rules,

222
00:08:48,161 --> 00:08:49,217
like the fund's,

223
00:08:49,217 --> 00:08:50,901
easier to keep.

224
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:53,340
But there is a warning sign.

225
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:56,139
The OECD says Norway's productivity growth

226
00:08:56,139 --> 00:08:58,428
is now among the lowest in the

227
00:08:58,428 --> 00:08:58,912
OECD,

228
00:08:58,912 --> 00:09:01,456
and its lead in living standards over

229
00:09:01,456 --> 00:09:03,975
other rich countries has narrowed,

230
00:09:03,975 --> 00:09:08,402
from about 42% to 27% in fifteen

231
00:09:08,402 --> 00:09:09,256
years.

232
00:09:12,717 --> 00:09:15,717
The first risk is the oil price.

233
00:09:15,717 --> 00:09:18,360
After the summer of twenty fourteen,

234
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:20,300
oil fell to around a third of

235
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,627
its level.

236
00:09:21,777 --> 00:09:25,068
The krone weakened by about 30 percent,

237
00:09:25,068 --> 00:09:29,130
and unemployment rose from 3.6 to 4.7

238
00:09:29,130 --> 00:09:30,197
percent.

239
00:09:30,450 --> 00:09:32,950
The second is time.

240
00:09:33,110 --> 00:09:35,065
More than half of Norway's known oil

241
00:09:35,065 --> 00:09:35,774
and gas,

242
00:09:35,774 --> 00:09:37,265
57 percent,

243
00:09:37,265 --> 00:09:39,820
has already been produced.

244
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:42,238
Output is forecast to fall by the

245
00:09:42,238 --> 00:09:43,629
end of the decade,

246
00:09:43,629 --> 00:09:45,515
as the world tries to move away

247
00:09:45,515 --> 00:09:47,059
from fossil fuels.

248
00:09:47,317 --> 00:09:49,587
The third is age.

249
00:09:49,707 --> 00:09:51,947
Today there are about three people of

250
00:09:51,947 --> 00:09:54,635
working age for every Norwegian over

251
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:55,907
sixty-five.

252
00:09:56,057 --> 00:09:57,601
By 2050,

253
00:09:57,601 --> 00:10:00,207
official projections imply about two.

254
00:10:00,207 --> 00:10:02,462
Pensions and care will cost more,

255
00:10:02,462 --> 00:10:05,346
just as oil money starts to shrink.

256
00:10:05,583 --> 00:10:08,726
And the fund itself is exposed to

257
00:10:08,726 --> 00:10:10,583
the world's markets.

258
00:10:10,733 --> 00:10:13,161
In the manager's own stress test,

259
00:10:13,161 --> 00:10:17,036
a fragmented world economy could knock 37

260
00:10:17,036 --> 00:10:19,000
percent off its value.

261
00:10:22,450 --> 00:10:25,490
So why is Norway so rich?

262
00:10:25,490 --> 00:10:27,620
Not just because it found oil.

263
00:10:27,690 --> 00:10:29,699
Because of what it decided to do

264
00:10:29,699 --> 00:10:30,500
next.

265
00:10:30,670 --> 00:10:33,150
It kept control of the resource.

266
00:10:33,150 --> 00:10:34,850
It taxed it heavily.

267
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,013
It saved the money abroad,

268
00:10:37,013 --> 00:10:39,422
and it spends only the return.

269
00:10:39,683 --> 00:10:42,423
The oil will run out one day.

270
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:44,962
The rules are designed so that the

271
00:10:44,962 --> 00:10:46,473
fortune does not.

272
00:10:46,653 --> 00:10:47,879
In the IMF's words,

273
00:10:47,879 --> 00:10:50,882
Norway faces the future from a position

274
00:10:50,882 --> 00:10:51,983
of strength.

275
00:10:52,033 --> 00:10:54,206
This is The Hidden Economics.
